From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: mpr, explorer: Map network drive and Disconnect network drive

David: "you should be able to map a drive in the file browser." Wine's
WNetConnectionDialog1W and WNetDisconnectDialog were stubs (WN_NO_NETWORK).
mpr now shows the dialogs Windows does: Map Network Drive -- a drive letter
(the free ones, last first), the folder (\\server\share, checked), Reconnect
at sign-in, Connect using different credentials (CredUI) -- connecting with
WNetAddConnection2W, the network provider's (wine-sg 0057); and Disconnect
Network Drives, the network drives by letter. File Explorer's "See more"
menu has both, as Windows 11's does; after a map it opens the new drive,
after a disconnect it leaves the drive for This PC, and This PC's branch of
the tree is read again.

Gate: make test-mapdrive (the dialogs; a real share is mapped and
disconnected on the QA VM).
